Relevant columns & how they will be used  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels.image_id`: joins to the `images` table.  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels.label_name`: filter to the cat class (`'/m/01yrx'`).  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels.confidence`: keep only rows where `confidence = 1`.  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images.image_id`: joins to the `labels` table.  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images.original_url`: the value we finally count (distinct URLs).  
• `bigquery-public-data.open_images.dict.label_name` / `label_display_name`: confirms that `'/m/01yrx'` really means “Cat”.  

Typical conditions  
```sql
WHERE l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND l.confidence = 1
```  
For the “other” set we need the negative condition, e.g.  
```sql
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` l2
                  WHERE l2.image_id = i.image_id
                    AND l2.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
                    AND l2.confidence = 1)
```

Below are ten illustrative queries (each limited to ≤20 rows) that move from simple inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Look‑up “cat” in the label dictionary.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.dict`
WHERE label_display_name = 'Cat'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Show raw label records that are “cat” with confidence 1.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
WHERE l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND l.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Distinct image‑ids that have a confident “cat” label.
SELECT DISTINCT l.image_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
WHERE l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND l.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Join those cat image‑ids to the images table to see URLs.
SELECT i.image_id, i.original_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`  AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels`  AS l
  ON i.image_id = l.image_id
WHERE l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND l.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Count distinct URLs that are “cat”.
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT i.original_url) AS cat_url_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`  AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels`  AS l
  ON i.image_id = l.image_id
WHERE l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND l.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;   -- (one row will return, so still within the rule)
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Total number of distinct image URLs in the whole images table.
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT original_url) AS total_url_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Cross‑check “cat” images using the bounding‑box table instead of labels.
SELECT DISTINCT a.image_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.annotations_bbox` AS a
WHERE a.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
  AND a.confidence = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Image‑ids (and URLs) that have NO confident “cat” label.
SELECT i.image_id, i.original_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT 1
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
      WHERE l.image_id = i.image_id
        AND l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
        AND l.confidence = 1)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Distinct “other” URLs (no cat label).
SELECT DISTINCT i.original_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images` AS i
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT 1
      FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
      WHERE l.image_id = i.image_id
        AND l.label_name = '/m/01yrx'
        AND l.confidence = 1)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final answer – count of cat URLs vs. other URLs.
SELECT
  SUM(CASE WHEN has_cat THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS cat_url_cnt,
  SUM(CASE WHEN has_cat THEN 0 ELSE 1 END) AS other_url_cnt
FROM (
  SELECT
    i.original_url,
    MAX(CASE WHEN l.label_name = '/m/01yrx' AND l.confidence = 1
             THEN TRUE ELSE FALSE END) AS has_cat
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`  AS i
  LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
    ON i.image_id = l.image_id
  GROUP BY i.original_url
)
LIMIT 20;   -- returns one summary row
```

Running query 10 will yield the two requested numbers:  
• `cat_url_cnt`  = count of distinct image URLs that contain a confident “cat” label.  
• `other_url_cnt` = distinct image URLs that never contain that label.
