Successfully corrected. SQL:
--Description:  Return TWO counts in one query, based on DISTINCT original URLs
--              from the Open‑Images dataset.
--              • cat_url_cnt   – # of URLs whose image_id has at least one label
--                                with label_name = '/m/01yrx' (Cat) AND confidence = 1.
--              • other_url_cnt – # of URLs whose image_id never has such a label.
--              ---------------------------------------------------------------
--              Steps inside the query:
--              1) Start from `open_images.images` (every image_id + original_url).
--              2) LEFT JOIN to `open_images.labels` so that images without any labels
--                 are still kept (needed to compute “other”).
--              3) For each URL, turn joined label rows into a numeric indicator:
--                   1 when (label_name = '/m/01yrx' AND confidence = 1), else 0.
--                 Taking MAX() of that flag per URL gives 1 if ANY qualifying
--                 row exists.  Convert the result to BOOLEAN → has_cat.
--              4) In the outer SELECT, COUNTIF(has_cat) gives the cat total,
--                 COUNTIF(NOT has_cat) gives the other total.
SELECT
  COUNTIF(has_cat)         AS cat_url_cnt,
  COUNTIF(NOT has_cat)     AS other_url_cnt
FROM (
  SELECT
    i.original_url,
    MAX(
      CASE
        WHEN l.label_name = '/m/01yrx' AND l.confidence = 1 THEN 1
        ELSE 0
      END
    ) = 1 AS has_cat
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_images.images`  AS i
  LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_images.labels` AS l
    ON i.image_id = l.image_id
  GROUP BY i.original_url
);
